 media projects as he had a humorous role  in the animated harley quinn series  vying for poison ivy's love as such this  reference may not be entirely lost on  everyone but even if you've never heard  of kite man you can probably figure out  what his power is it's just as  ridiculous as his name implies  kite man's entire superhero persona is  modeled around a kite he can fly or  glide like a kite and often employs  kite-related weaponry as a comic book  character he isn't well known and is  generally regarded as a charming relic  from a campier age of comic book  storytelling that said peacemaker at  least takes kite man seriously in  episode 5 peacemaker proudly displays  the newspaper clipping in his trailer  where he's hailed as a hero for  apprehending kite man while peacemaker  has been derided during the series as  being a wannabe superhero and even  sometimes a villain this clipping makes  it appear that he was once recognized as  a true blue good guy perhaps that's why  he keeps a reminder of this fond memory  in his trailer in the next episode he's  seen telling school children the story  of when he brought down kite man and  turned him in clearly his battle with  this less than nefarious villain is  something that gives him great pride  wouldn't he have crashed anyway due to  gravity  no  perhaps augie's elderly neighbor was  onto something peacemaker may kill his  enemies now but at one point he used to  operate as a straight arrow similar to  batman a hero he seemingly despises  midway through the series clemson mirn  makes a deal with a former comrade  casper lock to help tamp down calls for  reworking the evidence incriminating  peacemaker and lock poses as the new  police captain to accomplish this  however during locke's initial meeting  with mirn in episode 5 he references the  duo's past in the jungles of niacer  niacer is another fictional country in  dc lore located in northern africa it's  only been referenced during one story in  which superman travels to the country to  investigate a metahuman among the  membership of a church being suppressed  by the government when the military  takes part in killing missionaries the  metahuman known as redemption launches a  retaliatory attack superman comes to  blows with the character and redemption  proves to be able to handle himself  against the man of steel he can unleash  blasts of energy and maintain the same  level of strength as superman this could  just be a simple reference for fans to  consume or a potential narrative thread  that may bear fruits in the future only  time will tell  if the justice league exists in the dc  eu surely some of the other more famous  dc heroes like the green arrow do as  well in episode 8 the team sets off on  their noble mission to kill a cow which  is the food source of the series is  butterflies while devising a plan  peacemaker's anti-gravity helmet floats  away when the ota accidentally activates  it with a voice command though  frustrated peacemaker begins coming up  with a new plan coming up with the idea  to plant his sonic boom helmet on top of  the barn he mentioned shooting the  fishing line to the barn from the top of  one of the trees and letting the helmet  slide down the idea ends up reminding  vigilante of someone else like green  arrow no not like green arrow peacemaker  of course has just as much disdain for  green arrow as he does for every other  dc superhero even claims that green  arrow goes to brony conventions and  cosplays as the rear end of twilight  sparkle lyoto finally says what we're  all thinking by observing that  peacemaker has an absurd story for every  superhero either peacemaker is pretty  naive and genuinely believes everything  he reads on the internet or he simply  hates superheroes too much to care about  spreading false rumors honestly it's  probably both where do you get this  nonsense  google well it's not true you know more  than google well congratulations  all right this is likely one easter egg  nobody missed at the tail end of the  series the justice league does arrive at  the site of the butterflies clash with  peacemaker and crew but they're too late  while wonder woman and superman are  presented as conspicuous silhouettes  jason mamoa and ezra miller show up in  the flesh to reprise the roles of  aquaman in the flash aquaman even  hilariously drops an f-bomb as he  dismisses the rumors peacemaker's been  spreading about what he does with the  fish  i'm so  sick of that rumor  [Music]  it's  not a rumor  while it's obvious that henry cavill and  gal gadot did not show up for this  particular shoot day batman is curiously  absent from the lineup as well we know  that ben affleck is coming back as  batman for a final performance as a  character in the flash movie which  raises questions about why he didn't  show up here perhaps batman couldn't  arrive on the scene as fast as everyone  else this time regardless peacemaker  once again displays his disgust for the  team and doesn't even give them the time  of day the only people happy to see the  justice league in the show are  apparently the folks at home  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the dc extended universe are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

